5112,15.9,2011,22,80,29]],"links":[["Andrews County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/texas/andrews-county"],["ARC or PLC in Andrews County","/arc-plc/texas/andrews-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 42 of them. In 2025 that middle got 2% of normal in February to March and 43% in November to December. Every grid shown had its driest year in 2011, and grid 14809 got just 24% of normal that year. On grid 14512 the preliminary estimate for August to September 2026 sits at 27.5, and RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ.</p>"}
